.TH GIGACTL-GUI 1 "2026-07-25" "gigactl 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gigactl-gui \- GigaControl, the desktop app for Gigabyte G5/G6 fans and keyboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gigactl-gui
.br
.B gigactl-gui \-\-tray
.br
.B gigactl-gui \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B GigaControl
is the desktop front end for
.BR gigactld (8).
It shows live CPU and GPU temperatures, both fans' speed and duty cycle, and
lets you pick a fan profile, draw a custom fan curve, and set the keyboard
backlight's colour and brightness.
.PP
It is an unprivileged D\-Bus client: every change is a request to the daemon,
which authorises it through polkit and is the only process that touches the
Embedded Controller. The user of the active local session is not asked for a
password, as with screen brightness. Run it from your application menu as
.BR GigaControl ,
or from a terminal.
.PP
With a tray host present the window can be closed without quitting: the app
keeps running behind its tray icon, whose menu switches fan profile, toggles the
backlight and reopens the window. Closing the window with no tray host quits,
because nothing would be left to reopen it from.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start with no window, showing only the tray icon. This is what the autostart
entry uses at login.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH AUTOSTART
The package installs
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/gigactl-tray.desktop
so the tray starts at every login. To opt out, place a file of the same name
containing
.B Hidden=true
in
.IR ~/.config/autostart/ ,
or use your desktop's startup\-applications settings.
.SH THE TRAY ICON
The tray uses the StatusNotifierItem protocol. GNOME does not implement it
without an extension: on Ubuntu the preinstalled AppIndicator extension provides
it, and if nothing does, the app says so once and runs from its window alone.
KDE, XFCE, Cinnamon and MATE support it natively.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/io.github.smairio.gigactl.desktop
The application menu entry.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/gigactl-tray.desktop
The login autostart entry.
.SH NOTES
A machine outside the verified Gigabyte G5/G6/G7 range is reported as
unsupported in the window rather than refused, since the app itself writes
nothing; the daemon and the command line tools carry the guards.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gigactld (8),
.BR gfan (1),
.BR gkbd (1)
.PP
.UR https://github.com/smairio/gigactl
